within BobLib.Experiments.Standards;

model KnCLocked "Single-axle kinematics and compliance with a locked rack"

  extends BaseClasses.PartialKnC(final steerable = false);
  annotation(__OpenModelica_simulationFlags(nls = "kinsol"), experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 118, Tolerance = 1e-6, Interval = 1), Documentation(info = "<html><p>One replaceable axle with shared fixtures and measurements. Run one complete sweep at lockedRackPosition; steering sources are removed. Select front/rear data using useRearAxle. See BaseClasses.PartialKnC for the calibration and brake contracts.</p><h4>Numerical solver</h4><p>OMEdit selects <code>nls=kinsol</code> for the algebraic equilibrium equations. Pass <code>-nls=kinsol</code> explicitly when launching a native executable outside OMEdit. This is independent of the time integrator: the quasi-static rig has zero continuous states and OpenModelica uses Euler even if DASSL is requested. Wheel compliance uses the elastic implementation; body inertia and suspension damping are omitted by the rig.</p><p>With OpenModelica 1.27.1 on Linux ARM64, three complete compliant four-post runs gave median wall times of 6.071 s with homotopy and 1.125 s with KINSOL; the seven-angle compliant single-axle sweep gave 2.026 s with KINSOL. Full MAT output and existing tolerances were retained. Across both protocols, 36,414 sampled output/deflection comparisons agreed within 1.3e-9 maximum absolute difference. These measurements cover the tested bellcrank/stabilizer configuration, not every architecture or calibration, and are not real-time guarantees.</p></html>"));
end KnCLocked;
